# ImmutableStack Project Rules

## Project Overview
ImmutableStack is a comprehensive toolkit for creating applications with the "Immutable Stack" - Elixir/Phoenix backend with React/Redux frontend. It provides code generation, AI-powered file repair, and development tooling for full-stack applications.
## Project Structure
### Root Directory Structure
```
ImmutableStack/
├── assets/                    # Static assets (logo, images)
├── composite/                 # High-level generation orchestrators (see subfolder structure below)
├── generators/                 # Core code generation modules (see subfolder structure below)
├── injectors/                 # Code injection utilities (see subfolder structure below)
├── readers/                   # File parsing and data extraction
│   ├── genfile/              # Genfile parsing
│   └── get_app_data.ts       # Application data extraction
├── repair/                    # AI-powered code repair system
│   ├── adapters/             # LLM adapters
│   └── types/                # Repair type definitions
├── runners/                   # Command execution utilities
│   ├── nomix.ts              # Mix command execution
│   └── index.ts              # Execution orchestration
├── utils/                     # Shared utilities and helpers
│   ├── settings/             # Settings management
│   ├── chunk.ts              # Array chunking utilities
│   ├── format.ts             # Code formatting
│   ├── gen_header.ts         # File header generation
│   ├── history_cache.ts      # Generation history tracking
│   ├── logger.ts             # Custom logging system
│   ├── lorem.ts              # Lorem ipsum generation
│   ├── map.ts                # Mapping utilities
│   ├── path.ts               # Path utilities
│   └── string.ts             # String manipulation (Names utility)
├── immutable_*.ts            # Main entry point scripts
├── start.ts                  # Development environment setup
├── package.json              # Node.js dependencies and scripts
├── tsconfig.json             # TypeScript configuration
├── Vagrantfile               # Vagrant development environment
├── versions.sh               # Version definitions for asdf
└── dev_kit_macos.sh          # macOS development tools installation

### Subfolder structure
PARENT_DIR
│   ├── gen_channel/          # Phoenix Channel processes
│   ├── gen_phoenix/          # Phoenix-specific processes
│   ├── gen_react/            # React-specific processes
│   ├── init_configs/         # Configuration file processes
│   ├── init_docker/          # Docker file processes
│   ├── init_phoenix/         # Phoenix project setup processes
│   └── init_react/           # React project setup processes
│   └── add_api/              # API setup processes
│   └── add_worker/           # Worker setup processes
```

### Generated Project Structure (Output)
When ImmutableStack generates a new project, it creates:
```
GeneratedProject/
├── apps/
│   ├── app_name/             # Main Phoenix application
│   │   ├── lib/
│   │   │   ├── app_name/     # Core business logic
│   │   │   └── typescript/   # Generated TypeScript code
│   │   │       ├── requests/ # API request functions
│   │   │       └── state/    # Redux state management
│   │   └── test/             # Phoenix tests
│   └── app_name_web/         # Web interface
│       ├── lib/
│       │   └── app_name_web/
│       │       ├── controllers/ # HTTP controllers
│       │       ├── channels/   # WebSocket channels
│       │       └── router.ex   # Route definitions
│       └── test/
├── config/                   # Phoenix configuration
├── priv/
│   └── repo/
│       └── migrations/       # Database migrations
└── docker-compose.yml        # Docker development setup
```

Commands to run:
```
    Usage: 
      immutable -install                                # Install core (required)
      immutable -devkit                                 # Install external dev tools (optional)
      immutable -init _my_proj_name                     # Initialize a new project
      immutable -genfile _my_genname                    # Create a generator file
      immutable -gen _my_genfile_path                   # Run generator with generator file
      immutable -gen_channel _my_channel_name           # Create a channel
      immutable -repair _my_broken_file_path            # Repair a file using AI (see docs for details)
      immutable -gentemplate _my_genname _my_filepath   # Create a string literal template from existing code
      immutable -settings my_key: my_value              # Save a key:value to settings
      immutable -settings -clear                        # Clear local settings
      immutable -links                                  # Quick links to common files and directories
```

## Development Tools (Bash Functions)
```
    First:
        source ~/.bash_profile
    Usage:
      build                                            # Build ImmutableStack and homebrew-immutable packages
      init_proj <project_name>                         # Initialize new project with full build process
      gen <project_name> <genfile_name>                # Generate code using existing project and genfile
      version <version_number>                          # Update version across all package.json files and sync
```